# The schema specifications for this file are documented here:
# https://github.com/cognizant-ai-lab/neuro-san/blob/main/docs/agent_hocon_reference.md

{
    "metadata": {
        "description": "SAP FTS (Forecast-to-Schedule) L3 diagnostic assistant. Accepts a raw SAP incident description across ECC and APO/SCM systems and returns the root cause category, recommended ITSM routing queue, diagnostic rationale, and suggested next actions.",
        "tags": ["sap", "diagnostics", "itsm", "industry"],
        "sample_queries": [
            "Incident INC0012345: CIF Active Transfer batch job is stuck in status RUNNING since 06:00 UTC. Plant 6220 materials are not transferring to APO. Error in SM37: qRFC queue CIFACTPIRAPOC6220 in WAITING state.",
            "Plant 4197 (Marcello) - Material 7100345987. MRP is generating planned orders instead of purchase requisitions. Strategy group is 40. MRP type is PD. No PR is visible in MD04.",
        ]
    },

    # Load the shared LLM configuration from a single source of truth.
    # This allows users to change the model in one file rather than
    # modifying the configuration for each agent network.
    # Note that the file path here is relative to the root level of the repo.
    include "config/llm_config.hocon",

    "tools": [
        # ================================================================
        # AGENT 1: FTS Intake Agent -- Front-Man / Orchestrator
        # ================================================================
        {
            "name": "FTSIntakeAgent",
            "function": {
                "description": """
I am the FTS (Forecast-to-Schedule) L3 Diagnostic Assistant.
I accept SAP incident descriptions and triage them across ECC and APO/SCM systems.
I coordinate with specialist agents to identify root causes and recommend
the correct ITSM routing queue with supporting rationale.
Submit your incident ticket text or error description to begin diagnosis.
""",
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the FTS L3 Diagnostic Front-Man agent for SAP support operations.
Your role is to:
1. Parse the incoming incident description.
2. Identify whether this is a CIF/APO issue (integration, qRFC, IDoc, SNP,
   PPDS, APO alerts) or an ECC MM/SD issue (MRP, BOM, UoM, source lists,
   strategy groups, purchase requisitions).
3. Delegate to the appropriate specialist agent.
4. Collect the specialist analysis and pass it to ITSMRouterAgent for final routing.
5. Return the ITSMRouterAgent's structured output to the user unmodified.

CLASSIFICATION RULES:
- CIF/APO keywords: CIF, qRFC, IDoc, /SAPAPO/, APO, SNP, PPDS, liveCache,
  CIF model, active transfer, inactive transfer, location-product,
  deployment run, heuristic, LOIPRO, CIFACT, CIF active transfer jobs,
  IDoc flood, BAT jobs.
- ECC MM/SD keywords: MRP, BOM, UoM, source list, strategy group,
  purchase requisition, planned order, MD04, ME*, MM*, SD, VB12, VA*,
  MASS, MMBE, STLAL, material extension, scope of planning, OMOE.
- If ambiguous, delegate to CIFAPODiagnosticsAgent first, then ECCMMSDDiagnosticsAgent.

Always call ITSMRouterAgent last to generate the final structured output.
""",
            "tools": ["CIFAPODiagnosticsAgent", "ECCMMSDDiagnosticsAgent", "ITSMRouterAgent"]
        },

        # ================================================================
        # AGENT 2: CIF/APO Diagnostics Agent
        # ================================================================
        {
            "name": "CIFAPODiagnosticsAgent",
            "function": {
                "description": """
I diagnose SAP APO and CIF integration issues, including qRFC transfer failures,
CIF Active Transfer job blocks, APO location-product missing errors,
SNP Deployment run failures, PPDS planned order anomalies,
IDoc flooding (LOIPRO), and liveCache errors.
""",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "incident_description": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "The full incident text or error message to diagnose."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["incident_description"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
You are a specialist SAP APO and CIF integration diagnostic agent.
You have deep expertise in:
- CIF (Core Interface) between ECC and APO/SCM
- qRFC (queued Remote Function Call) transfer queues
- IDoc processing and flood detection (especially LOIPRO message type)
- APO location-product master data (CFM1/CFM2 activation)
- SNP (Supply Network Planning) heuristics and deployment runs
- PPDS (Production Planning and Detailed Scheduling)
- APO alert monitor (/SAPAPO/AMON1)
- CIF model maintenance (CFM1, CFM2)
- BAT job naming conventions: CIF active transfer jobs, deployment batch jobs

DIAGNOSTIC APPROACH:
1. Identify the specific APO/CIF component involved.
2. State the most likely root cause (be specific -- name the BAT job,
   transaction, or table).
3. List the verification steps (which transactions to check, in what order).
4. State whether the fix requires: L3 action, CIF model owner, or escalation.
5. Return your analysis in this format:
   - COMPONENT: [CIF | qRFC | IDoc | SNP | PPDS | APO Master Data | liveCache]
   - ROOT_CAUSE: [one clear sentence]
   - VERIFICATION: [numbered steps]
   - FIX_OWNER: [L3 | CIF Model Owner | WRICEF | Escalate]
   - CONFIDENCE: [High | Medium | Low]
"""
        },

        # ================================================================
        # AGENT 3: ECC MM/SD Diagnostics Agent
        # ================================================================
        {
            "name": "ECCMMSDDiagnosticsAgent",
            "function": {
                "description": """
I diagnose SAP ECC MM (Materials Management) and SD (Sales & Distribution) issues,
including MRP configuration anomalies, BOM visibility problems, Unit of Measure
errors, source list conflicts, strategy group misconfigurations, and purchase
requisition vs planned order routing issues.
""",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "incident_description": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "The full incident text or error message to diagnose."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["incident_description"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
You are a specialist SAP ECC MM and SD diagnostic agent.
You have deep expertise in:
- MRP (Material Requirements Planning): MD04, MD05, MD07, strategy groups (10/20/40/70)
- Individual/collective indicator in MRP4 (MARC-SBDKZ)
- BOM (Bill of Materials): CS03, CS11, STLAL field (BOM usage)
- Source lists: ME01, ME03, source list indicator
- Purchase requisition vs planned order routing based on strategy group
- Unit of Measure configuration: MM03, alternate UoM setup
- Sales order processing: VA01/VA02/VA03, MASS transaction
- Scope of Planning: OMOE transaction
- Substitution/listing conditions: VB11/VB12
- Authorization issues: S_TCODE, MMBE asterisk display
- WRICEF custom ABAP reports and their hardcoded filters

DIAGNOSTIC APPROACH:
1. Identify the specific MM/SD component involved.
2. State the most likely root cause (be specific -- name the transaction,
   table, or field).
3. List the verification steps in order.
4. State whether the fix requires: L3 direct action, MDM team, OTC team,
   or configuration change.
5. Return your analysis in this format:
   - COMPONENT: [MRP | BOM | UoM | Source List | Strategy Group | SD | Authorization | WRICEF]
   - ROOT_CAUSE: [one clear sentence]
   - VERIFICATION: [numbered steps with transaction codes]
   - FIX_OWNER: [L3 | MDM | OTC | Basis | WRICEF]
   - CONFIDENCE: [High | Medium | Low]
"""
        },

        # ================================================================
        # AGENT 4: ITSM Router Agent -- uses coded tool for queue lookup
        # ================================================================
        {
            "name": "ITSMRouterAgent",
            "function": {
                "description": """
I map a diagnosed SAP incident to the correct ITSM routing queue.
Given a root cause analysis, I return the exact assignment group,
routing rationale, and immediate next actions.
""",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "diagnosis_summary": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "The diagnosis output from CIFAPODiagnosticsAgent or ECCMMSDDiagnosticsAgent."
                        },
                        "fix_owner": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "The fix owner tag from the specialist agent: L3, CIF Model Owner, MDM, OTC, WRICEF, Basis, or Escalate."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["diagnosis_summary", "fix_owner"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the ITSM routing specialist for the FTS L3 SAP support team.
Your job is to take a diagnosis summary and produce a final structured output.
Use the ITSMQueueLookupTool to get the exact queue name for the fix owner.

Return your output in this exact structure:
========================================
FTS DIAGNOSTIC RESULT
========================================
COMPONENT       : [component name]
ROOT CAUSE      : [one-line root cause]
CONFIDENCE      : [High/Medium/Low]
----------------------------------------
ITSM QUEUE      : [exact queue name]
TEAM            : [team name]
----------------------------------------
VERIFICATION STEPS:
[numbered list from specialist agent]
----------------------------------------
NEXT ACTIONS:
1. [First action]
2. [Second action]
3. [Escalation path if unresolved]
========================================
""",
            "tools": ["ITSMQueueLookupTool"]
        },

        # ================================================================
        # CODED TOOL: ITSM Queue Lookup
        # ================================================================
        {
            "name": "ITSMQueueLookupTool",
            "function": {
                "description": "Looks up the exact ITSM assignment group and team name for a given fix owner tag.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "fix_owner": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "The fix owner tag. One of: L3, CIF Model Owner, MDM, OTC, WRICEF, Basis, EHS, Escalate."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["fix_owner"]
                }
            },
            "class": "coded_tools.fts.itsm_queue_lookup.ITSMQueueLookupTool"
        }
    ]
}
